      "reason": "Never executed before (validate-only failed since c17831a). Run as committed, the mutant never terminates: without the visited check FindPath re-enqueues around C->C/D->A and rebuilds the path through the C self-loop forever, so both Cycle_selfloop_and_order and the old positive control Shortest_directed_paths (same cyclic graph) hung until the runner's 600 s subprocess timeout, which is a runner failure, not a kill. The red test now decides the mutant by assertion on an acyclic diamond before any cyclic query, and gains the documented R-to-Y Unreachable/empty-proof check. The positive control is a path query that terminates under the mutant (single-edge PathAsync, also M11's control). The mutation itself is unchanged."
    }
